; A journal that is VALID — hledger accepts it, and so do we, with no
; diagnostics — and whose at-cost sum is nevertheless not zero.
;
; This is the fixture behind `BalanceSheetReport::balanced`. It reproduces the
; user-reported "assets − liabilities − equity should be zero, but it is
; $0.00227970" to the digit, and it is NOT a defect in this journal.
;
; Where the residue comes from
; ----------------------------
; A priced posting is worth `quantity × unit price` at cost, and `Dec`
; multiplication ADDS the scales: four decimal places of shares times four of
; price is eight places of dollars.
;
;   26.2690 VTI @ $289.7713  =  $7,612.00227970
;
; The cash that paid for it can only be written to the cent, so the surplus
; digits cannot be cancelled by anything a journal is able to say — there is no
; way to write $0.0022797 into a bank account. The residue is arithmetic, not a
; mistake, and it is unavoidable for any journal that records fractional lots.
;
; Why hledger says the file is fine
; ---------------------------------
; hledger's transaction-balance test tolerates half a unit at the precision the
; ENTRY was written at, which `parse::check_transaction_balances` reproduces
; (`looks_zero`). $0.0022797 is well under half a cent, so both tools accept it:
;
;   $ hledger -f fixtures/reports/bs-cost-dust.journal check
;   (silent, exit 0)
;
; hledger carries exactly the same residue internally and merely hides it behind
; two-decimal display. Forced to show it (hledger 1.52):
;
;   $ hledger -f fixtures/reports/bs-cost-dust.journal bal -B -c '$1000.00000000'
;         $2388.00000000  assets:bank:checking
;         $7612.00227970  assets:broker:vti
;       $-10000.00000000  equity:opening
;       ----------------
;            $0.00227970
;
; So the grouped balance sheet's `check` is right to report `$0.00227970`, and
; wrong to conclude from it that the journal does not balance. `check` stays the
; exact residual; `balanced` is the verdict, and it is true here because the
; residue is smaller than one cent — smaller than any posting that could exist.

account assets:bank:checking   ; type: C
account assets:broker:vti      ; type: A
account equity:opening         ; type: E

2026-01-01 opening balance
    assets:bank:checking        $10,000.00
    equity:opening             $-10,000.00

2026-02-01 buy a fractional lot
    assets:broker:vti            26.2690 VTI @ $289.7713
    assets:bank:checking      $-7,612.00
